WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.979
Imagine you're inviting a friend in Denver to

00:00:02.979 --> 00:00:05.958
your online book club. You wrote, Thursday at

00:00:05.958 --> 00:00:08.937
seven p.m. Eastern. The word Eastern matters. Your

00:00:08.937 --> 00:00:11.544
friend lives in a different time zone.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.911
You paste the invitation into your AI chat

00:00:21.911 --> 00:00:24.863
and ask, make this shorter. It replies, Book

00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:27.814
club, Thursday at seven! Would your friend know

00:00:27.814 --> 00:00:30.765
when to join? Read it once more. The

00:00:30.765 --> 00:00:31.872
time zone disappeared.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.057
Before fixing the invite, save a little note.

00:00:43.057 --> 00:00:45.994
Copy what you asked and the original invitation.

00:00:45.994 --> 00:00:48.931
Underneath, write what you needed: the shorter invite

00:00:48.931 --> 00:00:51.868
must still say Eastern. Now you have an

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.704
example you can use again.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.250
Try again with the original invitation. This time

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.259
say, shorten it and keep the time zone.

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:11.269
Suppose the reply says, Book club, Thursday at

00:01:11.269 --> 00:01:14.279
seven p.m. Eastern. Look for the word you

00:01:14.279 --> 00:01:16.160
wrote down. There it is.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.819
Your turn. Think of one AI reply you

00:01:27.819 --> 00:01:30.718
had to correct. What single detail was missing?

00:01:30.718 --> 00:01:33.618
Put the request and that detail together in

00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:35.792
a note. That's the whole tip.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.013
Keep that note for the next time you

00:01:45.013 --> 00:01:47.106
try a different way of asking. You'll already

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.198
know what a good answer needs to keep.

00:01:49.198 --> 00:01:50.768
See you in the next tip.
